    fix(aggregate): sanitize trace_steps before q_t curve in cross-family
    
    cross_family_analysis loaded trace_steps.csv raw and did groupby(step).correct.mean(),
    so hard-kill-corrupted rows (step=0, a confidence-like value in correct) inflated the
    accuracy curve -- e.g. llama x gpqa reported peak acc 24.23 at step 0. Apply the same
    _sanitize_step_frame guard, then regenerate all 4 aggregates. All peak accs now in [0,1].
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

